language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ mario: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Mario needs to collect as much gold as possible by visiting different houses. He starts at Mario's house and ends at Luigi's house, and the route closes with the travel from Luigi's house back to Mario's house. Each house has a certain amount of gold, and the travel between houses uses fuel. Mario has a limited amount of fuel, so he plans his route to maximise the gold collected without exceeding the fuel limit. Give, for each house, the house that succeeds it on the route; a house that is not on the route is its own successor.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `mario.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/mario.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `mario_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py mario.json
$   savilerow model.eprime mario_1.param -run-solver

$ nHouses: the number of houses
given nHouses : int
$ the house where Mario starts (houses are numbered from 0 in the data, so house h is model index h+1)
given marioHouse : int
$ the house where Luigi's route ends (numbered from 0 in the data)
given luigiHouse : int
$ the fuel Mario has
given fuelLimit : int
$ goldInHouse[i]: the gold in house i (house h of the data is model index h+1)
given goldInHouse : matrix indexed by [int(1..nHouses)] of int(0..)
$ arc_fuel[i,j]: the fuel used to travel from house i to house j (indices shifted as above)
given arc_fuel : matrix indexed by [int(1..nHouses), int(1..nHouses)] of int(0..)

$ s[i]: the house succeeding house i on the route, as a house number from 0 (the output); s[i] = i-1 when house i is not on the route
find s : matrix indexed by [int(1..nHouses)] of int(0..nHouses-1)
$ position[i]: the place of house i on the route, counted from Mario's house as 0 (0 for a house not on the route)
find position : matrix indexed by [int(1..nHouses)] of int(0..nHouses)
$ the total gold collected on the route
find total_gold : int(0..sum(goldInHouse))

maximising total_gold
such that
$ the successors are all different, so every house has exactly one predecessor on the route
allDiff(s),
$ the total gold is the gold of the houses on the route
total_gold = (sum i : int(1..nHouses) . toInt(s[i] != i-1) * goldInHouse[i]),
$ the fuel of the arcs of the route, including the arc from Luigi's house back to Mario's house, is no more than the fuel limit
(sum i : int(1..nHouses) . toInt(s[i] != i-1) * arc_fuel[i, s[i]+1]) <= fuelLimit,
$ Mario's house is on the route and the route leaves it
s[marioHouse+1] != marioHouse,
$ the route ends at Luigi's house, whose successor is Mario's house
s[luigiHouse+1] = marioHouse,
$ Mario's house is at position 0 of the route
position[marioHouse+1] = 0,
$ along the route each house is one place after its predecessor, except that Luigi's house closes the circuit back to Mario's house; so the route is a single circuit and no separate loop of houses is formed
forAll i : int(1..nHouses) . (((s[i] != i-1) /\ (i != luigiHouse+1)) -> (position[s[i]+1] = position[i] + 1)),
$ a house not on the route has position 0
forAll i : int(1..nHouses) . ((s[i] = i-1) -> (position[i] = 0))
